================================================================================
Bundled fonts
================================================================================

One font file is redistributed, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. The full
licence text, carrying the copyright notice below, is in licenses/OFL-1.1.txt.

  IBM Plex Sans    Copyright 2019 IBM Corp. (https://github.com/IBM/plex)
                   app/src/main/res/font/ibm_plex_sans_variable.ttf
                   Window Ver/src/main/resources/font/ibm_plex_sans_variable.ttf

  The copyright line is taken from the font's own name table (name ID 0), not
  transcribed by hand. Neither this font nor Geist below declares a Reserved
  Font Name, so the OFL's renaming clause does not bite.

The marketing site separately serves Geist (Copyright 2024 The Geist Project
Authors), also OFL-1.1, with its notice at website/fonts/OFL.txt. The website
is not part of the public source tree, but it is a public redistribution of the
font, which is what the OFL attaches to.

Everything else is set in the platform's generic serif family, which resolves to
a font already on the user's device (DirectWrite on Windows, the system serif on
Android). No serif font is bundled or redistributed by this project.


================================================================================
Bundled Java runtime (Windows installer only)
================================================================================

The Windows installer ships a trimmed Java runtime produced by jpackage from
Eclipse Temurin 17 (OpenJDK). It is not in this source tree; it is assembled at
package time and lives under runtime/ inside the installed application.

  Eclipse Temurin / OpenJDK 17    GPLv2 with the Classpath Exception
      The Classpath Exception is what permits linking and shipping the runtime
      alongside an Apache-2.0 application without the GPL reaching this code.
      Full text: https://openjdk.org/legal/gplv2+ce.html

jpackage carries the JDK's own legal/ tree into the runtime image, and the
installer copies the application directory recursively, so the licence texts
ship inside the install at runtime\legal\ (44 files). That is what satisfies
the GPL's requirement to accompany the binary — do not prune that folder to
save space.

This applies to the installer artifact, not to the source distribution.


================================================================================
Third-party dependencies
================================================================================

Declared in gradle/libs.versions.toml and resolved at build time; not
redistributed in this source tree. Notable licences:

  AndroidX, Jetpack Compose, Room, Kotlin, kotlinx.coroutines   Apache-2.0
  ZXing (barcode decoding)                                      Apache-2.0
  Gson                                                          Apache-2.0
  JUnit 4 (test scope only, not redistributed)                  EPL-1.0

  Facebook Shimmer for Android 0.5.0                            BSD-2-Clause
      Copyright (c) 2015, Facebook, Inc. Two clauses, not three — verified
      against the LICENSE file at the 0.5.0 tag, which also carries a separate
      PATENTS grant. Both texts are reproduced in
      licenses/BSD-2-Clause-shimmer.txt, because clause 2 requires binary
      redistributions to reproduce the copyright notice and disclaimer, and the
      Android app ships Shimmer compiled in.

  Java Native Access (JNA / jna-platform)      LGPL-2.1-or-later OR Apache-2.0
      JNA is dual-licensed and its POM states that either may be chosen. This
      project takes it under the Apache-2.0 option. No LGPL obligation
      therefore attaches to this distribution.

Every dependency above is open source. Google ML Kit Barcode Scanning, a
closed-source SDK, was removed on 30 Jul 2026 and its QR decoding replaced with
ZXing, which the project already used to generate the same codes. The dependency
tree carries no proprietary component.
